m2s-cfs patch for FreeRTOS-Kernel V11.3.2 (8a59a4b19bf72977819feddef87d41163ced7004)
File: portable/ThirdParty/GCC/Posix/port.c  (Linux simulator only; not used on the Cortex-M3 target)

Problem (measured 2026-11-03, see docs/test-results/03-freertos-posix-smoke.md):
  The tick thread is a loop of pthread_kill(SIGALRM) + usleep(1 ms). On the development VM
  usleep(1000) takes ~2.7 ms, so FreeRTOS time ran at 0.38-0.44x real time. Pending SIGALRMs
  also coalesce, so late ticks are lost for good.

Change:
  1. The tick thread sleeps to absolute 1 ms deadlines (clock_nanosleep TIMER_ABSTIME), so sleep
     overshoot does not accumulate.
  2. The SIGALRM handler computes the number of due ticks from CLOCK_MONOTONIC and calls
     xTaskIncrementTick() once per due tick; a context switch is done once if any call asked for it.
  3. prvStartTimeNs is set before the tick thread is created (it was set after).

Apply (never in sources/): patch -o <build>/port.c sources/FreeRTOS-Kernel/portable/ThirdParty/GCC/Posix/port.c <this file>

--- a/portable/ThirdParty/GCC/Posix/port.c
+++ b/portable/ThirdParty/GCC/Posix/port.c
@@ -111,6 +111,7 @@
